# Tensor product of modules over commutative ring
%%%
tag := "Chapter2/Exercise2.11.7"
number := false
%%%
**Exercise 2.11.7.** Show that if $`M` and $`N` are modules over a commutative ring $`A`, then $`M \otimes_A N` has a natural structure of an $`A`-module.
